# Backgrounds
@scenario tutorial_lesson_04
@include /definitions/characters.vns
@label start
[mode dialogue standard]
[set ui.dialogueUi project]
[bg room]
[char ginger global on]
[set ui.dialogueFadeMs 160]
[stage clear]
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: This studio starts with a blank wall. The script calls it room. What happens if you give that name a different picture?
ginger: Open scripts/definitions/characters.vns to see the image path. The bg command in this lesson selects it.
> Review question -> check
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label check
ginger: What belongs after bg?
> The name of the current speaker. -> retry
> The ID declared for the backdrop. -> correct
> Back to topics -> return_hub
@label retry
[show ginger guide confused]
ginger: The declaration maps an ID to an image. The scene command selects it. Give it another try.
[jump check]
@label correct
[show ginger guide normal]
ginger: The declaration maps an ID to an image. The scene command selects it.
> Back to topics -> return_hub
> Replay example -> start
@label return_hub
[if !tutorial_done_04]
[flag tutorial_done_04]
[inc tutorial_count]
[endif]
[stage clear]
[goto TutorialHub:topics_page_2]
